          "summary": "The set \\(\\WFF\\) of well-formed formulas is the smallest set of strings satisfying the following formation rules: \\begin{enumerate} \\item Every propositional variable \\(P\\in\\Prop\\) belongs to \\(\\WFF\\). \\item If \\(\\varphi\\in\\WFF\\), then \\(\\neg\\varphi\\in\\WFF\\). \\item If \\(\\varphi,\\psi\\in\\WFF\\) and \\(\\circ\\in\\{\\land,\\lor,\\to,\\leftrightarrow\\}\\), then \\((\\varphi\\circ\\psi)\\in\\WFF\\). \\item No string is a well-formed formula unless it is obtained by finitely many applications of the previous clauses. \\",
